WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.890
Hey this is Presh Talwalkar. A single alien lands on Earth. Every day after that each

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:15.550
alien on Earth undergoes a transformation, which could be any of the four equally likely events.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.860
The alien could die.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.700
The alien could do nothing.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:30.960
The alien could replicate itself, which
means there are two aliens in total.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:36.000
Or, the alien could replicate itself two
times, which means there are three aliens total.

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:44.560
What is the probability the alien
race eventually dies out and goes extinct?

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.399
This question is sometimes asked as an
interview question for technical jobs.

00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:54.930
Can you figure it out? Give this problem
a try

00:00:54.930 --> 00:01:01.270
and when you're ready keep watching the
video for the solution.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:10.200
Let's write "p" for the probability that an alien and all of
its descendants die out.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:17.200
The probability that one alien and all of its
descendants die out is "p".

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.400
The next day there are four equally likely events.
There's a 25% chance

00:01:22.409 --> 00:01:28.650
that this alien could die out. This means
there's a conditional probability of 1

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:35.250
that this alien and all of its
descendants die out. There is another

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.250
contingency where the alien does nothing.

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:42.360
Now the situation is exactly the same.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.740
This means the probability is still "p"
that this alien and all of its

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:53.130
descendants will die out. There is also a
25% chance the alien

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:59.460
will replicate itself so that there are
two aliens. Now each of these aliens will

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:06.090
have a probability "p" that this alien and
all of its descendants will die out. Each

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.959
of these lines of aliens will be
independent from each other.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:15.800
The probability that both of them die
and all of their descendants die out will

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:20.880
be the product "p" times "p" equals "p"
squared.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:31.480
In the final 25% case, the alien replicates itself two times. Each of these aliens has a probability "p" of

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:36.320
dying out and having all of their
descendants die out. Each of these

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.900
branches is independent from each other.

00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:46.380
The probability that all three die out
will be equal to "p" times "p" times "p"which is "p" cubed.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:54.520
If the probability is to exist, it must satisfy the following equation.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.180
The probability of an alien and all of its descendants dying out

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:05.720
has to be equal to 0.25 times the quantity 1 + "p" + "p squared" + "p cubed".

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:13.760
In the theory of statistical branching processes, the probability of extinction is equal to the smallest

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:20.570
positive root of this equation. This is
equal to the square root of 2 - 1,

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:24.800
which is approximately 41.4% and that's the

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:31.640
answer. Now to be comprehensive, we should
consider the other solutions to this

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:37.940
equation. One solution is negative and
that can be disregarded because the

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:43.700
probability cannot be negative, but the
other solution is equal to 1. This would

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.810
mean there's a probability of 1 that
it's surely going to happen that the

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.060
aliens will go extinct.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.170
How do we know that this is not the
solution, and that the correct solution

00:03:54.170 --> 00:04:01.370
is 41.4 percent? To figure that out we
have to dig deeper into the details and

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:07.100
consider the discrete version of the
problem. Let's write p sub k for the

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:11.180
probability of an alien and all of its
descendants dying out

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:18.410
in k days. Let's consider the
probability that an alien dies out in k

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:22.550
plus 1 days. There are four things that
can happen the next day.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:27.320
There's a twenty-five percent chance the
alien dies out in which case the

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:31.580
conditional probability of dying out in
k plus 1 days is equal to 1.

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:37.669
There's a twenty-five percent chance the
alien does nothing. Now one day has

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:42.560
already passed so in order for this
alien and all of its descendants to die

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:48.740
out in k plus 1 days, the next day this
alien and all of its descendants would

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:49.699
have to die out

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:55.970
in k days, it would have to be one day
less. The conditional probability here is

00:04:55.970 --> 00:05:02.060
p sub k. In the twenty-five percent
chance the alien replicates itself so

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:05.870
there are two aliens, each of these
aliens and all of their descendants

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.850
would have to die out in k days.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:15.440
This is a conditional probability of p
sub k squared. In the final case the

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:21.440
alien replicates itself two times and
each of these aliens and have a p sub k

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.690
chance that that alien and all
the descendants would die out in k days.

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:32.180
The probability of all of them dying out
would be the product which is p sub k cubed.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:37.190
Now one thing to notice here
is that the expected number of aliens

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:45.289
the next day is equal to 0 + 1 + 2 + 3
all divided by 4 this is equal to 1.5

00:05:45.289 --> 00:05:50.330
which is greater than 1, that means the
alien is more than replicating itself on

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:54.440
average, so we can expect that there's a
chance the aliens would survive; the

00:05:54.440 --> 00:06:00.680
probability of extinction should not be
equal to 1 it should be less than 1. So

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:06.050
how do we know this is true? We have this
recursive equation for the probability

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:10.669
the alien dies out in k plus 1 days in
terms of the probability that it would

00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:16.760
die out in k days. We're going to show
that this probability is always less

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:22.430
than or equal to the square root of
2 - 1. Now what's the probability

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:25.210
an alien would die out in exactly one
day?

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:29.900
Well that's only the 25%
chance that it simply dies out in the

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:31.070
following day.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.680
This is our base case. Now we assume this

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:40.770
is true for all values less than or equal [I correct myself to say] less than p sub k + 1.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:46.470
So we have this recurrence relation and
we can now apply the induction

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:51.600
hypothesis on all the terms p sub k. So we'll substitute in square root

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.650
of 2 - 1 for those terms, and this
all simplifies to be square root of

00:06:55.650 --> 00:07:01.590
2 - 1. So we have an increasing
sequence of p sub k because the

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:04.770
probability keeps increasing as we
expand the number of days.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.970
This is an increasing sequence and we
know it's bounded by square root of

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:14.070
2 - 1, so in fact this sequence
will converge to the value of

00:07:14.070 --> 00:07:18.870
square root of 2 - 1, and that in
fact is the correct answer to this problem.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.580
Did you figure it out? Thanks for
watching this video, please subscribe to

